Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 17:46:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 112/154] feat(settings): remove the window's macOS titlebar
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a chromeless style for the settings window (full-size content
view, transparent titlebar, hidden title) while keeping the traffic
lights and resize border. With no titlebar the WebView-filled window
had no drag handle, so its ClientView now answers NonClientHitTest
from the page's own -webkit-app-region regions, tracked through a
WebContentsDelegate that also keeps the existing key-forwarding
behavior.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
index e68bb4ef13e6f..26d90e9a71610 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
@@ -3615,6 +3615,8 @@ static_library("ui") {
       "atrium/atrium_surface_key_route_mac.mm",
       "atrium/atrium_surface_quit_route_mac.h",
       "atrium/atrium_surface_quit_route_mac.mm",
+      "atrium/atrium_settings_titlebar_mac.h",
+      "atrium/atrium_settings_titlebar_mac.mm",
       "atrium/atrium_peek_intercept.h",
       "atrium/atrium_peek_navigation_throttle.h",
       "atrium/atrium_settings_window.h",
